    "title": "Where to watch TCU basketball vs. Duke in the NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "March 21, 2026, 10:55 a.m. MTThe Big 12 is down to six teams in the NCAA Tournament following the opening round, and the conference owns one of the premier games of the Saturday slate, with No. 9 TCU set to take on the top overall seed, the Duke Blue Devils.Both TCU and Duke were pushed in their opening game, with the Horned Frogs going back and forth with Ohio State before eventually pulling out the narrow two-point victory.Duke, on the other hand, faced No. 16 Siena and was giving everything they could handle. The Blue Devils were down 11 points at halftime, a record deficit for a No. 1 seed against a No. 16 seed. Duke's defense and forward Cameron Boozer took over in the second half, leading the team to a 71-65 win.TCU, with top scorer David Punch, has better than a puncher's chance to knock off the Blue Devils despite being a double-digit underdog.Here's everything you need to know about how to tune into the second round matchup:TCU basketball vs. Duke: TV channel, tip timeDate: Saturday, March 21TV Channel: CBSStart Time: 5:15 p.m. CT, 3:15 p.m. MTThe Horned Frogs and the Blue Devils will tip off at 3:15 p.m. MT from the Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville, South Carolina.Where to stream TCU vs. DukeTCU-Duke will be available to stream on the NCAA March Madness app (with a TV provider login) and on Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers.Watch TCU vs. Duke in the NCAA Tournament on CBSContact/Follow us @BuffaloesWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook for ongoing coverage of Colorado news, notes and opinions.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
